step_details.raw_response:
Thought: Test a deterministic best_single strategy using the top model CWT_rf on the full pool to see if a single strong model outperforms the weighted ensemble.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"best_single","model":"CWT_rf","models":["CWT_rf","ARIMA","ETS","THETA","CWT_catboost","DWT_catboost","ONLY_CWT_rf","ONLY_FT_rf","NaiveMovingAverage"],"rationale":"check if the best model alone is superior"}

Thought: Test a robust alternative by using the median over the most stable pool (pool1) to see if it can beat or approach the best single model.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool1"}

Thought: Test a trimmed mean over the 9 most consistent models in pool3 to see if it improves on the best single CWT_rf.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool3","trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: Test a robust median over a slightly larger consistent pool (pool2) to see if expanding the subset improves robustness.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool2"}

Thought: Try a trimmed‑mean over the full model pool to see if including all models with trimming improves robustness.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool_full","trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: Test DTW barycenter over the more stable pool1 to see if it improves over median/trimmed_mean on that subset.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool1","dba_max_iter":30}

Thought: Test best_single CWT_rf within the more stable pool1 to see if restricting to top 5 models improves robustness.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"best_single","pool":"pool1","model":"CWT_rf"}

Thought: Test a robust median combination on the larger pool4 to see if expanding the pool improves over median pool1.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool4"}

Thought: Test best_single CWT_rf on pool2 to see if expanding the pool improves over the current best single model while keeping the same model choice.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"best_single","pool":"pool2","model":"CWT_rf"}

Thought: Test a simple mean over pool4 to see if a narrower pool improves robustness beyond the best single.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool4"}

Thought: Test a trimmed‑mean over the more focused pool4 to see if trimming improves over the plain mean on that subset.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","models":["ARIMA","ETS","THETA","CWT_rf","CWT_catboost","DWT_catboost"],"trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: Test a robust median over pool3 to see if a different pool improves over median pool4.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool3"}

Thought: Test a trimmed‑mean over pool4 (9 models) with 20% trimming to see if trimming improves over plain mean and median on that subset.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool4","trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: Try a simple mean over pool5 to see if a slightly larger, more diverse pool improves over mean pool4.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool5"}

Thought: Test a DBA combination on the moderately diverse pool2 to see if iterative reweighting improves over the best single.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool2","dba_max_iter":30}

